# Go Module Dependencies (Cursor)

Applies to every `Games-Labs-*/`, `api-gateway/`, and other Go service directories in this monorepo.

## Never commit local replace

- Do **not** add or keep `replace github.com/SparqLab/shared-lib => ../shared-lib` (or any `replace`) in committed `go.mod`.
- Use a **locked** `require github.com/SparqLab/shared-lib v0.0.0-...` from the module registry.
- For local monorepo work without editing `go.mod`, use `go.work` — not `replace`.

## After any go.mod change

When you **remove replace**, **bump shared-lib**, or change any `require`:

1. Run in the **affected service directory only** (not repo root):

```bash
cd Games-Labs-Missions   # example
GOWORK=off GOPRIVATE='github.com/SparqLab/*' GONOSUMDB='github.com/SparqLab/*' go mod tidy
```

2. **Commit `go.mod` and `go.sum` together** before push.
3. Verify the same constraint CI/Docker uses:

```bash
GOWORK=off go build -mod=readonly ./...
```

Do not consider dependency work done until `-mod=readonly` passes locally.

## Why this is mandatory

- Dockerfiles and CI use `go build -mod=readonly` — they **cannot** fix a stale or missing `go.sum` at build time.
- Typical failure: `missing go.sum entry for module providing package github.com/SparqLab/shared-lib/...`

## Agent checklist before finishing

- [ ] No `replace` directive in committed `go.mod`
- [ ] `go mod tidy` run in the correct sub-project
- [ ] `go.sum` updated and staged with `go.mod`
- [ ] `go build -mod=readonly ./...` passes in that service
